docs/planning/decisions.md-529-## D035 — Reviewed Runtime writes with an AppKit confirmation and secret sheet
docs/planning/decisions.md-530-
docs/planning/decisions.md-531-Decided in C09 (implementer decision, recorded for review).
docs/planning/decisions.md-532-
docs/planning/decisions.md-533-- C09 implements exactly v1's Runtime write subset (`bridge/src/protocol.ts`
docs/planning/decisions.md-534-  allowed matrix at 74754c02): profiles and custom topics create, update and
docs/planning/decisions.md-535-  delete; applications update and delete; API keys create, version, rotate
docs/planning/decisions.md-536-  and delete; never force delete. v1's validation, authorship (the
docs/planning/decisions.md-537-  management client ID), key-creation checks (application and key names
docs/planning/decisions.md-538-  case-insensitively unique over a 40×25 walk, the one deployment profile's
docs/planning/decisions.md-539-  auth code injected by the desktop), baseline and review digests, typed
docs/planning/decisions.md-540-  confirmation ("CREATE" or the item name) and impact text are kept. Request
docs/planning/decisions.md-541-  bodies are normalized with the SDK's own request contracts
docs/planning/decisions.md-542-  (`scm_sdk::validation::parse`), the Rust counterpart of v1's zod parse.
docs/planning/decisions.md-543-- The SDK has no conditional-write precondition, so a change re-reads its
docs/planning/decisions.md-544-  baseline immediately before writing and refuses (not sent) when the
docs/planning/decisions.md-545-  review digest differs, as v1 did; a 409 is a conflict. An external writer
docs/planning/decisions.md-546-  can still race the final read; atomic conflict prevention is not claimed.
docs/planning/decisions.md-547-  Writes are never retried; a transport failure's outcome stays unknown.
docs/planning/decisions.md-548-  After a write the item is read back by the operation (v1 relied on the
--
docs/planning/decisions.md-2356-   result. That result is the inline check's grading verdict, progress
docs/planning/decisions.md-2357-   cleared by a course reset, and certificates unchanged across it. The
docs/planning/decisions.md-2358-   runner already supports these assertions (`call.*` entries take
docs/planning/decisions.md-2359-   `?? <pointer> …` expectations, tested); the 2.1.0 work designates and
docs/planning/decisions.md:2360:   runs them. C25 stays complete at its D034 chunk gate. The P08 phase
